      "message": "I found that dav1d validates a nonzero operating_point_idc this way, and I seem to remember Ronald Bultje discussed this check with me.\n\ndav1d/src/obu.c:\n\n```\n        hdr-\u003enum_operating_points \u003d dav1d_get_bits(gb, 5) + 1;\n        for (int i \u003d 0; i \u003c hdr-\u003enum_operating_points; i++) {\n            struct Dav1dSequenceHeaderOperatingPoint *const op \u003d\n                \u0026hdr-\u003eoperating_points[i];\n            op-\u003eidc \u003d dav1d_get_bits(gb, 12);\n            if (op-\u003eidc \u0026\u0026 (!(op-\u003eidc \u0026 0xff) || !(op-\u003eidc \u0026 0xf00)))\n                goto error;\n```\n\nDo you remember what libgav1 does?",
      "revId": "23049353c61be25575bdb408c9769fe350bd99e1",
